+## 2026-10-18 continuation: implementation and acceptance status
+
+The 2026-10-18 isolated worktree extends the initial prototype with an auditable blind-review evidence bundle, matched R1/R2 pairing and sibling cancellation, explicit unverified-narrative labels, a source-free Provider connectivity probe, and an append-only human case-decision gate. These paths keep Agent findings candidate-only; confirmed/reportable case status requires a human decision tied to case evidence and a completed same-case validation whose gate passes and reachability is verified. The live API smoke on loopback 18880 used a temporary repository/data directory: scan, candidate-to-case linking, evidence attachment, JSON/Markdown export and human-candidate update succeeded; a confirmation without runtime validation returned 409. Scan and case vulnerability counts stayed zero. The isolated server/Workers were stopped, and existing services were left untouched. Browser interaction was not tested because Work browser automation is disabled.
+
+The paired experiment requires one static-only R0 record, matching repository/commit/report/source identity and equal provider/model/implementation/prompt/tool/budget settings before it queues R1 and R2. Blind export is only available after all reviews and session closure; hashes bind the packet, reviewer record and result package. Synthetic reviewer records are workflow fixtures, not human labels. The Provider probe is operator-triggered and source-free; no real Provider request has been made. Real model efficacy, precision/recall and product vulnerability status therefore remain unknown.
+
+## 2026-10-18 continuation: detector-obligation review matrix
+
+Each model result now includes exactly one indexed disposition for every static evidence obligation: `evidence_found`, `contrary_evidence`, or `unresolved`. The server enforces complete, unique index coverage and requires a bounded verbatim citation for the first two dispositions. Unresolved rows may remain uncited. These labels represent model triage only: server validation checks coverage and quote presence, not semantic support. The result, case export, blind packet, and assessment panel carry the matrix and its limitation; prompt and tool-policy versions were bumped so older consent fingerprints cannot authorize this payload shape. An empty citation set is reported as `no_citations`.
+
+Validation: focused Agent workflow tests passed 39/39; full Python suite passed 851 tests with 5 Docker-only skips; Web tests passed 16/16; TypeScript `tsc --noEmit`, production build, Python compile, and `git diff --check` passed. The static fixture R1/R2 runner completed with 1/3 Fake calls and candidate-only outputs. The pinned `security_access_token` rerun used commit `17d88bfb36bea6c9370ba919ac41a22d16dd66b3`, eight detectors, 16 diagnostics, and four complete obligation rows per arm; R2's fixed-commit quote passed the service check. New result: `research/deliveries/agent/agent-investigation-20261018/pinned-source-fake-obligation-smoke-20261018.json`. All experiments used a Fake Provider with zero network calls; no human review or independent vulnerability ground truth exists. Both arms stayed candidate with `validated_vulnerability=0`. These results test wiring and schema enforcement only, not model accuracy or product vulnerabilities.
+
