+## Markdown report untrusted-text injection regression
+
+A review found that case Markdown export interpolated free-form Agent text, source quotations, and reviewer notes directly into Markdown. A model summary containing a newline and a fabricated `## CONFIRMED` heading, or image/link syntax, could therefore distort the exported report even though the text was labeled unverified. The exporter now collapses untrusted values to one line and escapes Markdown control characters for model text, citations, scanner metadata, and human notes. JSON retains raw model text with its provenance; the React panel and offline review form continue to render it as text. An end-to-end Fake Provider regression exercises heading, image, link, claim, and next-step payloads and confirms that the Markdown report keeps them inert while preserving the candidate-only gate.
+
+Validation after this change: the full Python suite passed 861 tests with five skips; Python compilation and `git diff --check` passed. This mitigates report-format injection; it does not establish semantic citation support or model accuracy.
