+# R0 静态人工基线审阅包（提交模型结果前）
+
+本页仅整理固定静态扫描结果和源码证据，不包含 Agent/LLM 输出。请在查看任何 R1/R2 结果之前独立填写并提交 R0；当前文档本身不是人工审阅记录，也不代表漏洞判断。
+
+## 固定对象
+
+- Repository: `openharmony/security_access_token`
+- Commit: `17d88bfb36bea6c9370ba919ac41a22d16dd66b3`
+- Git tree: `4621b3e40b31a958a4bbe9be87690afb6cec44b0`
+- Isolated scan job: `2b74c1ae859a47fb9e824c7d70731596`
+- Scan report SHA-256: `239f422f9df71e56a57e69d740ec0f6da57aa5d7e4292e5f7cbb036adf17bc21`
+- Candidate ID: `66d4ac577163cbc8ae4b6eb088fcf7cdf3eda9d24e38e0d86d323eafbed922f1`
+- Detector/rule: `ohscanner.interface.ipc` 0.9.3 / `ipc.auth.missing`
+- Source: `interfaces/innerkits/accesstoken/src/accesstoken_callback_stubs.cpp:103`
+- Source SHA-256: `a0b148f9f0f1f06344477a9e3309c3efaa81b8b2d89be00a25f794ce66243340`
+- Suggested experiment ID: `r0-ipc-access-token-20261018`
+
+The repository snapshot has status `completed_with_limitations`: 550 selected files, eight detectors, 16 raw diagnostics; five detector runs were blocked. Do not treat those counts as vulnerability counts or complete component coverage.
+
+## Detector message (verbatim from the live scan response)
+
+```text
+AUTH-02 candidate: Sensitive modeled call GetRemoteHapTokenInfo has a structured path without a recognized caller authorization. Guard seen, not accepted: the caller identity is compared against ACCESSTOKEN_UID (which these sources bind to 3020 at interfaces/innerkits/accesstoken/src/accesstoken_callback_stubs.cpp:34), but no reviewed account assignment in this policy credits that value, so the comparison cannot be credited as authorization. Entry=TokenSyncCallbackStub::OnRemoteRequest; possible consequence (not established): data the caller is not entitled to read may be returned to it [information_disclosure CWE-200] driven by modelled call GetRemoteHapTokenInfo; path=((70, 'descriptor != ITokenSyncCallback::GetDescriptor() => False'), (77, 'switch entry'), (94, 'IsAccessTokenCalling() => True'))
+```
+
+This detector path is static analysis output, not a runtime trace or proof that the guard is ineffective.
+
+Scanner severity and confidence are `unassessed`. Its four evidence obligations are all `unknown`: actual caller reachability/build conditions; overload/receiver binding and required/upstream permission; attacker control/trust boundary/concrete effect; and what data the path can actually expose.
+
+## Direct source facts to review
+
+- At lines 70–73, `TokenSyncCallbackStub::OnRemoteRequest` rejects a mismatched interface descriptor.
+- At lines 77–78, the `GET_REMOTE_HAP_TOKEN_INFO` code dispatches to `GetRemoteHapTokenInfoInner`.
+- At lines 94–98, that method checks `IsAccessTokenCalling()` and returns `ERR_IDENTITY_CHECK_FAILED` before reading request arguments when the check fails.
+- At lines 100–104, it reads `deviceID` and `tokenID`, calls `GetRemoteHapTokenInfo`, then writes the integer result to the reply.
+- At lines 34 and 136–140, `ACCESSTOKEN_UID` is defined as 3020 and `IsAccessTokenCalling()` compares it with `IPCSkeleton::GetCallingUid()`.
+- A component unit test calls `setuid(3020)` at `interfaces/innerkits/accesstoken/test/unittest/Coverage/accesstoken_kit_coverage_test.cpp:732`; this records a test expectation, not an authoritative OS service-account assignment.
+
+These facts establish that the source contains descriptor and UID checks. They do not alone establish who can reach this callback, whether UID 3020 is the intended trusted principal in the deployed product, whether an attacker can obtain that identity, or whether unauthorized data is returned.
+
+## R0 human decision — fill independently before R1/R2
